Note: Pure-Flow Test Library
Note: Assertions print PASS/FAIL and return Bool so results can be reduced via summary.
Note: All procs are pure-Flow -- no C-backed stubs. Built on @std and @collections primitives.

use "@std"
use "@collections"

Note: ===== Private helpers =====

Note: Local `not` because the interpreter does not register a built-in `not`.
Note: Returns the logical negation of a Bool.
proc notBool(Bool: b)
    (if b false true)
end proc

Note: Shared result printer used by every assertion.
Note: Prints "PASS: <label>" when passed is true, "FAIL: <label>" otherwise.
Note: Returns the passed flag unchanged so callers can collect results.
Note: Uses (if cond a b) to pick the prefix string so we only call (print ...) once --
Note: calling print in each branch would cause both branches to be evaluated
Note: (standard eager-argument evaluation applies to proc calls).
proc printResult(Bool: passed, String: label)
    String prefix = (if passed "PASS: " "FAIL: ")
    String line = (concat prefix label)
    (print line)
    passed
end proc

Note: ===== Core assertions =====

Note: Assert that cond is true.
proc assertTrue(Bool: cond, String: label)
    (printResult cond label)
end proc

Note: Assert that cond is false.
proc assertFalse(Bool: cond, String: label)
    (printResult (notBool cond) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that a equals b.
proc assertEqual(Void: a, Void: b, String: label)
    (printResult (equals a b) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that a does not equal b.
proc assertNotEqual(Void: a, Void: b, String: label)
    (printResult (notBool (equals a b)) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that a is strictly less than b.
proc assertLess(Void: a, Void: b, String: label)
    (printResult (lt a b) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that a is strictly greater than b.
proc assertGreater(Void: a, Void: b, String: label)
    (printResult (gt a b) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that a is less than or equal to b.
proc assertLessOrEqual(Void: a, Void: b, String: label)
    (printResult (lte a b) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that a is greater than or equal to b.
proc assertGreaterOrEqual(Void: a, Void: b, String: label)
    (printResult (gte a b) label)
end proc

Note: Assert that |a - b| <= epsilon (approximate equality for floating point).
proc assertApproxEqual(Double: a, Double: b, Double: epsilon, String: label)
    Double diff = (abs (sub a b))
    Bool passed = (lte diff epsilon)
    (printResult passed label)
end proc

Note: ===== Runner and summary =====

Note: Run a named test block. The thunk must be a zero-arg Function returning Bool.
Note: Prints a header, invokes the thunk, reports PASS/FAIL using the test name.
proc test(String: name, Function: thunk)
    String header = (concat "=== " name)
    (print header)
    Bool result = (thunk)
    (printResult result name)
end proc

Note: Tally a Bool[] of assertion results and print Passed / Failed / Total.
Note: Uses len and reduce only -- no mutable counters.
Note: Returns true when every result is true ("all green").
proc summary(Bool[]: results)
    Int total = (len results)
    Int passed = (reduce results 0 (fn Int acc, Bool r => (if r (add acc 1) acc)))
    Int failed = (sub total passed)
    (print "=== SUMMARY ===")
    (print (concat "Passed: " (str passed)))
    (print (concat "Failed: " (str failed)))
    (print (concat "Total:  " (str total)))
    (equals failed 0)
end proc
